.TH AD-COMPUTE 1 "2026-08-18" "ad 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ad_compute \- external diff computer for the ad toolkit (C++ implementation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_compute
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ad_compute
.B \-\-diff
.RI <patchfile>
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ad_compute
.B \-\-diff
.B \-
.RI <outputfile>
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ad_compute
.B \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_compute
is the external diff computer used by
.BR diffvim (1)
(via the --precomputed flag).
A single implementation exists in C++:

.TP
.B ad_compute
C++17 implementation. Source:
.IR compute/cpp/ad_compute.cpp .
Binary:
.IR bin/ad_compute .

The historical C, Rust, and Go variants were removed during the
Phase A refactor \(em the C++ tool is the only compute implementation
that remains. When the C++ binary is not on disk,
.BR ad_pipeline (1)
falls back to the pure-Perl
.I compute/perl/compute_builtin.pl
(a thin wrapper around
.IR DiffVim::Parser::Perl ).

The tool reads two files (or a unified diff) and writes a precomputed
diff file in the line-oriented format that
.B "diffvim --precomputed FILE"
consumes.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I oldfile
Old version of the file (two-file mode).
.TP
.I newfile
New version of the file (two-file mode).
.TP
.I outputfile
Where to write the precomputed diff.
.TP
.I patchfile
A unified diff file to read instead of two separate files (with
.BR \-\-diff ).
Use
.B \-
to read the diff from stdin.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm patience
Diff algorithm (default:
Patience).
(Myers was removed: it OOMs on 15K-line files and produces the same
op count as patience.)
.TP
.B \-\-word-diff
Batch word runs in char ops (instead of one char per op).
.TP
.B \-\-optimize-sequence
Reorder ops within a line so deletes come before inserts (default:
.IR on ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-optimize-sequence
Disable op reordering within a line.
.TP
.B \-\-left-to-right
Within each line, emit keeps (in original order), then deletes,
then inserts. Useful for left-to-right reading flow.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Read a unified diff instead of two files. Positional args become
(patchfile, outputfile).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. All options are set via CLI flags (see OPTIONS
above). For persistent defaults, use the config file at
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ad/config (defaults to ~/.config/ad/config).

.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
The output file is line-oriented:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# algorithm <name>
# word_diff <0|1>
# optimize_sequence <0|1>
# left_to_right <0|1>
# hunk_count <N>
HUNK <line>
keep|delete|insert <code>
HUNK <line>
keep|delete|insert <code>
...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where
.I code
is the Unicode code point of the character (e.g. 97 for 'a', 10 for
newline). See
.I docs/PARSERS.md
for a full description of the format.

.SH TIMING OUTPUT
Timing information is printed to stderr:
.PP
.RS
.nf
compute: <ms> ms (total)
startup: <ms> ms (process start to first byte read)
.fi
.RE

.SH BUILD
.PP
.RS
.nf
make -C compute cpp     # build the C++ variant (the only one)
make -C compute         # alias for the above
make -C compute benchmark OLD=... NEW=...
.fi
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_compute old.py new.py /tmp/diff.txt
Compute the diff and write to
.IR /tmp/diff.txt .
.TP
.B ad_compute --diff patch.diff out.txt
Read a unified diff and convert to diffvim format.
.TP
.B ad_compute --diff - out.txt < patch.diff
Read the diff from stdin.
.TP
.B bin/ad_compute old.py new.py /tmp/diff.txt && diffvim --precomputed /tmp/diff.txt old.py new.py
Compute the diff with the C++ tool, then run diffvim with the precomputed file.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR ad_compare (1)
.br
.I docs/PARALLEL_COMPUTE.md
covers the architecture, parallelism opportunities, and benchmark
results.
.I docs/PARSERS.md
documents the output file format in detail.
.I docs/src/architecture.md
has the mdBook version.
